window.EN={"1":"With Roy and the Lycian alliance army's retaking of the Etrurian capital Aquleia as the spark,","2":"one after another, the other Etrurian factions that had been watching and waiting turned against the coup faction.","3":"Chancellor Roartz and Western Isles Governor-General Arcardo and the rest of the coup faction were driven out of Etruria,","4":"and fled to the region of Ilia, which lay under the control of the Kingdom of Bern.","5":"The region of Sacae is a vast grassland spreading across the center of the continent; until Bern allied with some of its tribes and invaded,","6":"various tribes had been living a peaceful nomadic life, moving from place to place.","7":"The Kingdom of Etruria had been liberated, and under King Mordred,","8":"formed a coalition army together with Roy and the Lycian Alliance,","9":"and marched into Ilia to pursue the coup faction.","10":"At the same time, in order to solve the root of the problem, they decided to also attack the Kingdom of Bern lying behind it.","11":"Roy, not wanting to stand in the shadow of the Lycian Alliance, and also considering the effect on Etruria's knightly orders and the like,","12":"deliberately chose to call it the \"Etrurian Army,\" becoming commander of the coalition force.","13":"With the cooperation of the Church of Elimine, they set out on the expedition.","14":"But in addition to the temperament of the people of Sacae, who would not tolerate another nation's intrusion,","15":"the largest tribe, the Djute, had been brought under the command of General Brunnya, one of Bern's Three Dragon Generals,","16":"and so her formidable Bern western army stood in Roy and company's way.","17":"In the midst of all this, Roy and his group, as night fell, approached the border between Etruria and Sacae.","18":"...In other words, you're saying Narcian fell at Aquleia.","19":"Yes. It seems there's no mistake about it.","20":"I see...","21":"B-Brunnya, my lady... What's going to become of us?","22":"Don't worry.","23":"I won't abandon those who have cooperated with me.","24":"That much I, Brunnya, promise in the name of Bern's Three Dragon Generals.","25":"Oh, how grateful I am...","26":"Lord Arcardo, I'll leave Taras to you. Lord Roartz, I'll leave the land of Bulgar to you.","27":"I'll entrust each of you with your own.","28":"Wha— Wait just a moment!","29":"So close to the capital, the enemy will come attacking right away, won't they!","30":"Then you'll just have to repel them.","31":"Also, being close to the capital is convenient when the time comes to go on the attack.","32":"T-that's... true, but...","33":"Bulgar is the land of the foreign nation Sacae... I hear the nomads' resistance there is fierce...","34":"Isn't making them submit exactly the kind of thing your skill is for?","35":"Mmm...","36":"I hear that the enemy general, some boy called Roy, rebuilt the Lycian Alliance that we had crushed,","37":"and overcame countless plots besides, growing into the force he is today.","38":"Compared to that, the two of you now are practically living in heaven, aren't you?","39":"Ugh...","40":"Well then, I'll take my leave.","41":"I pray that you'll manage to retake Etruria.","42":"......","43":"...Are you certain about this?","44":"To cowards who abandoned their own country and fled in shame,","45":"there's no reason to show them any more favor than is necessary.","46":"They ought to be grateful I'm lending them land and troops at all.","47":"......","48":"We'll soon be at Etruria's border.","49":"Thank you so much, truly, for everything, Priest Yodel.","50":"Thanks to you and the Church of Elimine, the preparations for the expedition went off without a hitch.","51":"Not at all. If Lord Roy hadn't retaken the capital Aquleia for us,","52":"we'd still be suffering under Bern's oppression even now, I'd say.","53":"When you think of it that way, this much is nothing.","54":"I'm glad I could be of help.","55":"Lord Roy, actually, there's something I wanted to ask of you, if I may.","56":"What is it? If it's something I can do...","57":"If, where you're headed from here, you learn anything new about the \"dragons\"...","58":"I understand. I'll let Priest Yodel know each time something comes up.","59":"I'm grateful! I'll be counting on you.","60":"Oh, and there's one more thing I must tell you.","61":"As for the terrain around here, the roads grow narrow, hemmed in by mountains.","62":"And right now, it's night...","63":"In other words, the perfect spot for an ambush.","64":"Yes. Past the road between the mountains lies Taras Castle, which is under Bern's control.","65":"Understood. I'll make sure to proceed carefully.","66":"Well then.","67":"May fortune in war, and the blessing of the holy maiden Elimine, be upon the Etrurian army!","68":"You folks... are you going to fight against Bern's army?","69":"If so, please, take this staff with you.","70":"They say it's a staff that some famous princess once used...","71":"Well, well. It's rare for anyone to come all the way out to this backwater.","72":"What? The enemy's been eyeing this place?","73":"I see... Then I must thank you properly.","74":"Now, there should have been something here, a book for research purposes...","75":"Among Bern's soldiers, there was one strange fellow mixed in.","76":"That one's surely a thief.","77":"If we don't do something about it soon, the village is going to be in trouble, isn't it?","78":"Way, way to the northeast, there's supposed to be a village.","79":"From here, it's too far, so nobody's ever been there.","80":"I wonder if anyone's even living there after all?","81":"Wh— Why has it come to this!","82":"[If attacked with Klein] You, Klein! Betraying me, of all people—","83":"It's you who betrayed the nation of Etruria.","84":"Lord Arcardo!","85":"[If attacked with Douglas] Ge— General Douglas!","86":"So you ended up turning traitor to the enemy too? Damn you!!","87":"I... I am a... noble of Etruria.","88":"In... in a place like this... guh!...","89":"Lord Arcardo...","90":"Even someone who once served as Governor-General of Etruria's Western Isles,","91":"meets such an anticlimactic end in the end.","92":"Yeah... A year ago, we couldn't have imagined we'd be standing here like this now either.","93":"Maybe that's just how people's fates are.","94":"And that goes for the King of Bern too, I'd think...","95":"...Oh my, Lord Roy, that thing you're holding in your hand, what is it, might I ask?","96":"This? They say this is the \"Fire Emblem.\"","97":"My, my, this little jewel is...","98":"I was entrusted with it by Princess Guinivere.","99":"When she handed it over to me... she looked really pained.","100":"I bet, right up to the end, she wanted to make King Zephiel reconsider...","101":"Hmm... the bond between brother and sister, is it?","102":"Honestly, I'd always thought it a rather unreasonable thing to hope for.","103":"Why's that?","104":"The other party is none other than Bern's King Zephiel!","105":"After all, he's a man suspected of even having laid hands on his own father.","106":"For him to be moved by family ties is... hardly likely.","107":"Wh— What did you say! His own father?","108":"Oh my, did Lord Roy not know?","109":"Zephiel came to sit on the throne as the current king through the death of Bern's previous king.","110":"As for the previous king of Bern, his death was so sudden","111":"that all sorts of dark rumors have been circulating.","112":"And one of those is that his own son, the current king Zephiel...","113":"Assassinated him, yes.","114":"...I wonder if Princess Guinivere knows about that.","115":"That she wouldn't know at all seems... quite unlikely.","116":"......"};
